      <div type="commentary">
        <p n="1">The framed manuscript page number [ⲓⲏ] stands at the left on this page and is printed with a bar above and below as the frame, not as a supralinear stroke.</p>
        <p n="7">The bracket is not closed in the edition; it is closed here at the line end.</p>
        <p n="8">The bracket is not closed in the edition; it is closed here at the line end.</p>
        <p n="9">The edition opens a bracket at the end of the line; the lost letters and its closing bracket are in l. 10.</p>
        <p n="10">The lost section at the start of the line is opened by a bracket at the end of l. 9; it is closed here after the dots.</p>
        <p n="12">After ϩⲁⲗϭ the edition prints a closing bracket with no opening bracket on this line; the dots before it are encoded as illegible. At the line end the edition opens a bracket; its closing bracket is in l. 13.</p>
        <p n="13">The lost section at the start of the line is opened by a bracket at the end of l. 12; it is closed here after the dots.</p>
        <p n="15">Lines 15–16: the editors print, with a brace over both lines, "einstweilen unlesbar" (illegible for now); no text is given.</p>
        <p n="16">See l. 15.</p>
        <p n="19">The bracket before the last letters is not closed in the edition; it is closed here at the line end.</p>
        <p n="24">Lines 24–30: the editors print, with a brace over all seven lines, "einstweilen unlesbar" (illegible for now); no text is given.</p>
        <p n="25">See l. 24.</p>
